WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.800
Speaker 1: with an update on the&nbsp;
Russian invasion of Ukraine. Because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.400
yeah, there's been less media coverage of&nbsp;
this, but that doesn't mean there aren't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.440
newsworthy things happening. And it is going&nbsp;
so poorly, according to new reports for Russia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.560
that there are renewed questions as to whether&nbsp;
Putin is, quote, doomed, which we will get to in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.720
a moment, Reuters and others. But we'll look at&nbsp;
a Reuters report reporting that Russian troops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.680
are fleeing and getting back over the border&nbsp;
into Russia. Russia has largely ceded its gains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.360
near Kharkiv, writes Reuters. And many of the&nbsp;
withdrawing Russian soldiers have exited Ukraine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.600
moving over the border back into Russia.&nbsp;
This is per a senior U.S. military official.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.040
As it pulls back, the U.S. has seen anecdotal&nbsp;
reports of Russian forces abandoning equipment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.200
Again, disorganized command and&nbsp;
control, as mentioned. That's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.920
that that's been a hallmark, a&nbsp;
staple of Russian activity so far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.760
The remarks to Pentagon reporters followed a&nbsp;
weekend of rapid gains for Ukrainian forces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.880
Ukraine's general staff said its soldiers had&nbsp;
recaptured more than 20 towns and villages in just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:10.640
the last day as Ukrainian forces swept deeper into&nbsp;
territory seized from fleeing Russian troops. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:17.360
the big stories here were, of course, a war of&nbsp;
aggression by Russia. That's an accurate and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:24.960
true story. Expectations early that this would be&nbsp;
a very easy military win for Russia. Very quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.640
that assumption evaporated. However, there&nbsp;
was the belief that although on the one hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.160
the longer it went, the worse it is for Russia,&nbsp;
that eventually, if Russia decided to commit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:42.320
the resources, it would overwhelm Ukrainian&nbsp;
troops. That's not happening. And in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.360
things are going in the opposite direction. The&nbsp;
U.S. military official reads the same article, was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.360
upbeat but cautious when describing the Russian&nbsp;
advances. It's clear they're fighting hard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:57.600
Ukraine said it repelled attempted Russian&nbsp;
advances in two important areas of the Donetsk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:03.360
region, the city of Barmouth and Maersk,&nbsp;
near the coal producing town of Horlivka.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.480
The general staff said in an evening update. But&nbsp;
the senior U.S. official said Russia was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:15.040
focusing its firepower on Bermuda. So a lot more&nbsp;
tactical information that you can read, if that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.560
interesting to you. Now the question becomes what&nbsp;
about the propaganda war and what about the future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:26.480
of Vladimir Putin? There's an interesting article&nbsp;
in The Hill which is worth reading. If not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.800
it's worth reading, let's just put it that&nbsp;
way. And it's it's by Alexander Motul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.600
who's an opinion contributor, and it says,&nbsp;
like his soldiers, is Putin doomed? Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.560
the article is somewhat hyperbolic, admittedly,&nbsp;
and the article writes, Vladimir Putin is kaput.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:48.160
The proof of that is the below letter written&nbsp;
by a 26 year old soldier in the Russian army,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:53.920
Vivi Tarasenko. We know nothing about Tarasenko,&nbsp;
except he was a resident of Putin's brainchild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.680
the so-called Luhansk People's Republic, and that&nbsp;
he has a wife, Valeria, and a small son. We also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.800
know Tarasenko died in battle during the recent&nbsp;
Ukrainian offensive in the Kharkiv province.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:10.640
Ukrainian intel found the letter. The letter was&nbsp;
written with little punctuation and no capital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:16.000
letters. So the letter reads. This letter is for&nbsp;
the future if I should die or be taken prisoner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:22.400
or become a vegetable. Written July 17th, 2022.&nbsp;
It's very hard to write. I'm crying, but I must,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.080
beloved. Lera, tell our son what kind of dad I&nbsp;
was, that we were sent as cannon fodder to Zalman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:33.680
a village in Kharkiv province, without armor,&nbsp;
without ammunition, without normal weapons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.400
This is about our situation. When our son&nbsp;
grows up, tell him his dad wanted very much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:44.640
to return home to be the best dad ever. I've been&nbsp;
drinking and I'm writing emotionally. I know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.560
this all will be forgotten and that you will&nbsp;
be living your own life. That you'll find a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:52.960
new husband. That I'll simply disappear in&nbsp;
the war like all the guys. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.520
I didn't have a normal life. Say that Dad&nbsp;
was an athlete, didn't smoke, didn't drink.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.000
It's terrible that everyone has forgotten me. It's&nbsp;
very hard to accept all this. But all people die&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:08.480
and this cycle can't be changed. It's bad to die&nbsp;
in the summer. If only I were at the seashore. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:15.840
what is written in this Hill article is that&nbsp;
Tarasenko complaints are not unique. The Russian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.600
leadership with Putin at the head has evinced a&nbsp;
profoundly cavalier attitude towards lives not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.680
just of innocent Ukrainians, but also of Russian&nbsp;
soldiers. And what this article and others go on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:35.920
to say is that there is really no path out of this&nbsp;
for Putin. That is going to be anything short of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:42.320
of a failure and doom for Putin. Now, earlier,&nbsp;
there were all of these speculations as Putin's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:48.640
sick and has a death wish and is determined to be&nbsp;
assassinated eventually by operatives from other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:57.920
countries. Or is Putin so drunk on the idea of&nbsp;
reassembling some version of the USSR that he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:03.840
not thinking clearly? And whatever the case may&nbsp;
be, I at this point think the ship has sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.560
sailed on making rational sense out of what Putin&nbsp;
was thinking and when he was thinking it and what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:16.240
the end goal is here. But it is clear that if&nbsp;
there is going to be a win for Russia. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:24.720
going to be a win only with completely revised&nbsp;
objectives. And so at this point. When this didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:31.920
end in two weeks, we started talking about, well,&nbsp;
it's likely going to be more than months at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:36.880
point. And what is the ultimate goal? Because a&nbsp;
complete and total takeover of takeover of Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:43.440
seems increasingly unlikely. It seems quite&nbsp;
plausible that Putin and his cronies will revise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:49.520
their military objectives and they will revise&nbsp;
them to say, our goal is actually to control a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:57.600
lot less territory than we initially planned. With&nbsp;
those revised objectives, they may be able to come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:03.520
away with something that they would call a win&nbsp;
for propaganda purposes. But there's also a fear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:11.840
The fear is that as Russia and Putin realize,&nbsp;
we're not going to be able to continue mounting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:18.480
offensives and really take Ukraine in the way that&nbsp;
originally some projected us to do. There's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:25.760
fear that an increasingly belligerent Putin will&nbsp;
resort to those tactical nuclear weapons. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:32.080
are sometimes called battlefield nuclear weapons.&nbsp;
It's not like the massive bomb that destroys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:40.000
entire cities, but they are battlefields or&nbsp;
tactical nukes. And that that would be something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:47.040
that Putin is willing to do to kind of maintain&nbsp;
this image of strength, the kind of harebrained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:54.000
caricature of the alpha male that has pervaded the&nbsp;
MAGA movement in the United States. Quite frankly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.040
it's sort of a similar dynamic that is a fear&nbsp;
that an increasingly cornered Putin would go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.120
in that direction. So it is unpredictable&nbsp;
what is going to happen. But what we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:07.200
is that it is not going well for Russian&nbsp;
troops and there is still an invasion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:13.040
there is still a war, even if more and more a&nbsp;
mainstream corporate media isn't talking about it.

